virglrenderer: an unused first vertex input no longer leaves old attributes bound

What: when the vertex shader does not read its first input (no attribute
location for in_0), vrend now goes on to the next attribute instead of
returning from the vertex setup. Every attribute the program reads gets the
guest's new buffer, and attributes left unset are disabled. The same for a
vertex type vrend could not translate (refused when the elements are created,
so it should never get there).
Why: the early return ("Shader probably didn't compile - skipping rendering")
did not skip anything: the draw still went out with the previous draw's
attribute pointers and enabled mask. No GL call failed, so the pre-draw error
check saw nothing, and the draw range checks look at the guest's new buffers.
A guest could make the GPU fetch past an older, smaller buffer (second review
of gpu-robust, repro 5: a vertex shader that declares IN[0] and IN[1] and reads
only IN[1], after a draw that put a 16-byte buffer on location 0, read 64 bytes
from it). A shader that failed to compile never reaches this code; its draws
are dropped earlier (virgl-shader-failure-skip-draws.patch).
Upstream: upstream bug in vrend_draw_bind_vertex_legacy (used when the host GL
has no ARB_vertex_attrib_binding, as on macOS); upstreamable; not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-gpu-ranges.c case 35 (drawn, from the new buffer; the
oracle aborted before this patch).
--- a/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
+++ b/src/vrend/vrend_renderer.c
@@ -5546,19 +5546,20 @@
             loc = ctx->sub->prog->attrib_locs[i];
          } else loc = -1;
 
+         /* An input the shader never reads has no location. The draw goes on, so
+          * never return here: the attributes after it must still be set, and the
+          * enabled mask below must be updated, or the GPU fetches from the buffers
+          * of the draw before, which the draw range checks never saw. */
          if (loc == -1) {
             virgl_warn("%s: Cannot find loc %d %d %d\n", ctx->debug_name, i, va->count, ctx->sub->prog->ss[PIPE_SHADER_VERTEX]->sel->sinfo.num_inputs);
-            if (i == 0) {
-               virgl_warn("%s: Shader probably didn't compile - skipping rendering\n", ctx->debug_name);
-               return;
-            }
             continue;
          }
       }
 
+      /* refused when the vertex elements were created; left disabled if it ever gets here */
       if (ve->type == GL_FALSE) {
-         virgl_warn("Failed to translate vertex type - skipping render\n");
-         return;
+         virgl_warn("Failed to translate vertex type - attribute %d left disabled\n", i);
+         continue;
       }
 
       glBindBuffer(GL_ARRAY_BUFFER, res->gl_id);
